36,1,1,talk,Mio,,"Good morning, everyone! I hope you all had sweet dreams! I'm so curious—did our Seer find any spooky clues last night? Does anyone want to share what they've noticed so far?","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,1,1,talk,Misaki,,"Good morning. As we discussed yesterday, the Seer should be cautious about revealing themselves. However, if anyone has noticed any suspicious behavior or feels it is safe to share a lead, now is the time to speak.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,1,1,talk,Jonathan,,"Good morning. I agree with Misaki; we must balance the need for information with the necessity of safety. I have not noticed anything overtly suspicious yet, but I am listening closely to how everyone responds this morning.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,1,1,talk,Kenji,,"Good morning! I'm ready to help! I haven't seen anything weird yet, but I'm keeping my eyes wide open! @Mio, do you think the Seer will tell us something? I'm so excited to find the wolf!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,1,1,talk,Benjamin,,"Good morning. The air is thick with anticipation, is it not? While I share Kenji's curiosity, I wonder if the Seer's silence is a shield of prudence or a mask for a result that is... inconvenient.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,1,2,talk,Mio,,"@Benjamin, you're so mysterious! ""Inconvenient"" sounds so scary! Hehe. I'm just a regular girl, so I'm a bit lost. @Misaki, @Jonathan, do you think we should wait for the Seer, or start guessing who's acting weird?","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Benjamin"",""Misaki"",""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,1,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Mio, guessing without evidence is a gamble we cannot afford. We should wait for a claim or a contradiction. If we act on mere intuition, we risk executing an innocent villager and aiding the werewolf.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,1,2,talk,Jonathan,,I agree with Misaki. A gamble is far too risky when the stakes are so high. Let us continue to observe the dialogue; the truth often reveals itself in the gaps of a forced narrative.,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,1,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Misaki, @Jonathan, you're right! We shouldn't just guess! But it's so hard to just wait! @Benjamin, do you think someone is acting weird already? You always notice things that I miss!","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Misaki"",""Jonathan"",""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,1,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Kenji, you are far too kind. As for ""weirdness,"" it is often the most seamless performances that are the most suspicious. I find the current harmony quite... polished. I wonder who is most eager to maintain this peace.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,1,3,talk,Mio,,"@Benjamin, you're making me feel like we're all acting! Hehe. I'm just trying to be friendly! But if the harmony is too polished, maybe we should stir things up a bit? Does anyone actually feel suspicious of someone?","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,1,3,talk,Misaki,,"@Mio, stirring things up for the sake of it can be counterproductive. However, @Benjamin's insistence that our harmony is ""too polished"" is an interesting observation. I am curious if anyone is intentionally mirroring others to blend in.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Mio"",""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,1,3,talk,Jonathan,,"@Misaki, that is a keen observation. Mirroring is indeed a common tactic for those wishing to remain invisible. I wonder if the werewolf is currently hiding behind a facade of agreement to avoid drawing any attention to themselves.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,1,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Misaki, @Jonathan, mirroring? That sounds like a super cool detective trick! I'll try my best to just be myself! But wait, if the wolf is hiding by agreeing, does that mean we shouldn't trust each other? That's so sad!","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Misaki"",""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,1,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Kenji, sadness is a heavy burden, but trust is a currency we must spend wisely. It is not that we cannot trust, but that we must verify. I wonder if our ""detectives"" are perhaps too synchronized in their logic.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,1,4,talk,Mio,,"@Benjamin, you're always questioning everything! It's like a puzzle to you! But @Misaki and @Jonathan are just being helpful. If we can't trust logic, what can we trust? I'm getting a little confused! Who should we vote for?","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Benjamin"",""Misaki"",""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,1,4,talk,Misaki,,"@Mio, we can still trust logic, but we must apply it to everyone, including those who advocate for it. Since no one has claimed Seer and there are no contradictions, any vote today is a risk. I suggest we proceed with extreme caution.","{""words"":43,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,1,4,talk,Jonathan,,"I agree with Misaki. Without a clear lead, a rash decision could be fatal. However, we must eventually act. I suggest we reflect on who has been most eager to deflect suspicion before we cast our votes.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,1,4,talk,Kenji,,"@Jonathan, that's a scary way to think! I don't want anyone to be gone! But if we have to vote, I'll just trust you guys. I'm too nervous to pick! Does anyone have a real clue?","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,1,4,talk,Benjamin,,"A real clue is a rare jewel in such a polite gathering. Since we lack a Seer's revelation, we must look at the architecture of our conversation. I find the seamless alignment of Misaki and Jonathan quite... convenient. Shall we see who blinks first?","{""words"":44,""mentions"":[""Misaki"",""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
